                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "31ef6cbd-2c87-3015-ab17-fd19cb649d05",
                        "entry_id": "3af244d9-21bc-319e-a820-b0c620009ab7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To inhabit a place in unpleasantly large numbers; to plague, harass."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6107fceb-0fc2-4f1f-91c1-dcfbce3504df",
                                "sense_id": "31ef6cbd-2c87-3015-ab17-fd19cb649d05",
                                "text": "Insects are infesting my basement!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94919843-7b1b-4caf-a0df-42c02d1a9c05",
                                "sense_id": "31ef6cbd-2c87-3015-ab17-fd19cb649d05",
                                "text": "Sir, my liege,\nDo not infest your mind with beating on\nThe strangeness of this business; at pick’d leisure\nWhich shall be shortly, I’ll resolve you,\nWhich to you shall seem probable, of every\nThese happen’d accidents; till when, be cheerful\nAnd think of each thing well."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76e37dc3-76a3-4782-b236-9d7a029d60c9",
                                "sense_id": "31ef6cbd-2c87-3015-ab17-fd19cb649d05",
                                "text": "I come now to speak of the Pyrates infesting the West-Indies, where they are more numerous than in any other Parts of the World, on several Reasons […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b8d64f2-469c-468c-9a4e-6977a122b6a9",
                                "sense_id": "31ef6cbd-2c87-3015-ab17-fd19cb649d05",
                                "text": "It has often happened, that whole caravans have perished in crossing those deserts, either by the burning winds that infest them, or by the sands which are raised by the tempest, and overwhelm every creature in certain ruin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b37a49fa-ca25-46e5-8257-101beeafc4ac",
                                "sense_id": "31ef6cbd-2c87-3015-ab17-fd19cb649d05",
                                "text": "Nor was the biscuit much better; nearly all of it was broken into hard, little gunflints, honeycombed through and through, as if the worms usually infesting this article in long tropical voyages had, in boring after nutriment, come out at the antipodes without finding anything."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6e3c572c-19d9-3ad9-8ba5-b4713e679f49",
                        "entry_id": "3af244d9-21bc-319e-a820-b0c620009ab7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To invade a host plant or animal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a parasite"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
